{"severity":"error","file":"errors/overlapping_impl_1.march","start_line":22,"start_col":2,"end_line":22,"end_col":32,"message":"Two different types named `Stream_Message` both derive Json: `Stream_Message` (here) and `Stream_Msg.Stream_Message` (at errors/overlapping_impl_1.march:17:2).\n`from_json` picks its decoder by the result type's short name, so it cannot tell these two apart and would decode with the wrong one. Rename one of the types, or derive Json for only one of them.","code":"json_derive_name_collision","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/overlapping_impl_1.march","start_line":17,"start_col":2,"end_line":19,"end_col":5,"message":"`Stream_Msg.Stream_Message` derives Json here"}],"notes":[]}
{"severity":"error","file":"<none>","start_line":29,"start_col":778328713,"end_line":29,"end_col":168627782,"message":"Overlapping implementation: `impl JsonTo(Stream_Message)` conflicts with the implementation at <none>:29:997744773 — their heads overlap.\nA type may implement an interface at most once (coherence). If you meant a different behavior, wrap the type in a newtype and implement the interface on that.","code":"overlapping_impl","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
{"severity":"error","file":"<none>","start_line":126,"start_col":836750816,"end_line":126,"end_col":883194369,"message":"Overlapping implementation: `impl JsonFrom(Stream_Message)` conflicts with the implementation at <none>:126:599576702 — their heads overlap.\nA type may implement an interface at most once (coherence). If you meant a different behavior, wrap the type in a newtype and implement the interface on that.","code":"overlapping_impl","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
